.TH CHTTPCLIENT_RESP_HEADER 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpclient_resp_header \- look up a response header by name
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpclient.h>

const char *chttpclient_resp_header(const chttpcli_response *resp,
                                    const char *name);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function gives the value of the response header with the name
that you give, or NULL if that header is not there. The lookup ignores
the case of the name: the response stores each header name in
lowercase, and the function makes your name lowercase before the
lookup.

A server can send one header name on several lines. For such a name
the function gives the combined value that RFC 9110 section 5.3
defines: every value in the order of the wire, joined with ", ".
Set-Cookie is the one exception, because RFC 9110 section 5.3 and RFC
6265 section 3 forbid that combination for it (a cookie value can
itself hold a comma), so for "set-cookie" the function gives the first
occurrence. chttpclient_resp_header_count and
chttpclient_resp_header_at give every occurrence separately. The
headers map of the response holds the same value for each name.

The pointer that the function gives back stays valid until a call to
chttpclient_resp_free.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
resp  The response to query. It can be NULL, and the function then
      gives NULL.
name  The header name. It can be NULL, and the function then gives
      NULL.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A pointer to the value string of the header, or NULL if the function
does not find that header.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The map behind this function comes from the header block of the
response alone. A chunked response body can carry trailer fields (RFC
7230 4.1.2), which the client parses and validates, but they are not
response headers. A trailer field with any name therefore reads as
absent here, and such a field cannot replace a header that the server
really sent.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpclient_resp_header_count (3),
.BR chttpclient_resp_header_at (3),
.BR chttpclient_resp_free (3)
